      <tei:div type="colophon" subtype="introduction">
        <tei:p>A prayer, inspired by Tefilat haDerekh and other traditional liturgical texts, for a Jew who, at some future point, would be about to go forth on a starship. Doesn’t include a chatimah so as not to be a <tei:hi rend="italic">brakhah levatalah</tei:hi>, in the case that starships are (<tei:hi rend="italic">ḥas v’shalom</tei:hi>) never invented. Though written largely in jest/as an experiment, I was still somewhat moved when writing this, so I’ve dedicated it to the memory of the great Leonard Nimoy <tei:hi rend="italic">z”l</tei:hi>.</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
      <j:endConditional target="#osp_19657_introduction"/>
    </tei:front>
